{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>When a soul presents.</b> A person's soul. He mentioned \"soul\" because the meal offering is a freewill offering, and the soul too is called a freewill offering — \"and a willing spirit sustain me.\"" "<b>Fine flour.</b> Clean wheat flour. It is what is called in the language of Kedar samid. And behold, it is not fitting to be an offering to the Most High except from the kind than which there is none higher."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:27.137411952Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}